ttps://academy.investinglive.com/?utm_source=investinglive&amp;utm_medium=menu&amp;utm_campaign=get-certified)\n\n- More\n\n[![](https://investinglive.com/images/investing-live-logo.svg)](https://investinglive.com/)\n\n- [Live Feed](https://investinglive.com/live-feed/)\n- [Brokers](https://investinglive.com/directory/)\n- Livebytes\n\n- More\n\n[Home](https://investinglive.com/)\n\nTrump weighs another strike on Iran as Hormuz shipping risks mount. Returns to Washington after overseas trip.\n\n# Trump weighs another strike on Iran as Hormuz shipping risks mount. Returns to Washington after overseas trip.\n\n[News](https://investinglive.com/news &quot;News&quot;)\n\n[Greg Michalowski](https://investinglive.com/author/greg-michalowski)\n\n2 hours ago, published 19/11/2026 at 06:39 PM\n\n- Tags\n- [USD](https://investinglive.com/Tag/usd &quot;USD&quot;)\n\n[Add as a preferredsource on Google](https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=investinglive.com)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Reports Trump is in no rush to decide. Oil traders are watching whether the larger flow through Hormuz holds as reports of attacks on ships raise fresh concerns.\n\n![Trump](https://investinglive.com/cms/media/Processed/Categories/featured/2026-11-19_11-34-29-featured-1795113299.jpg?width=768&amp;format=webp)\n\nGeopolitics is building as President Trump is heading back to Washington after wrapping up talks with Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin in Shenzhen. Ukraine was a focus coming out of the meetings.\n\nOf course Iran is also a continued focus.\n\n#### With Xi, Iran, Hormuz, Taiwan and trade.\n\nTrump said he and Xi agreed that Iran should fully reopen the Strait of Hormuz and should not acquire a nuclear weapon. Trump also urged China to help end the war in Ukraine. Beijing’s readout emphasized Taiwan and Xi’s call for better communication on trade and economic issues.\n\n#### With Putin, a possible path to ending the Ukraine war.\n\nUkraine came up in Trump’s one-on-one with Putin and again in the three-way talks. Afterward, US envoy Jared Kushner said Russia was comfortable with the idea of NATO-style security guarantees for Ukraine. Putin separately ruled out direct talks with Kyiv, citing Ukraine’s strike on the Kerch Bridge\n\n#### With all three, nuclear risks and energy supplies.\n\nThe leaders agreed to hold talks on reducing nuclear risks and preventing proliferation. They also called for increasing supplies of refined petroleum products and keeping energy flows stable. The joint declaration gave no production targets or timeline and made no mention of either war.\n\n#### Trump is weighing his options on Iran\n\nUS President Donald Trump is considering another strike on Iran, Israel’s Channel 12 reported, citing an Israeli source. The broadcaster said Trump is in no rush to make a decision and that any strike would be carried out in cooperation with Israel. It said potential targets could include nuclear facilities, infrastructure and senior officials.\n\n#### Hormuz is the immediate focus for oil traders\n\nUS Energy Secretary Chris Wright said Wednesday saw by far the largest flow out of the Strait of Hormuz. Separately, i24NEWS, citing unnamed sources, reported that Iran had become more aggressive in recent days and was using cruise missiles against ships passing through the strait. The report did not provide details on which vessels were affected or whether they sustained damage.\n\nThe Houthis also said on Telegram that they would release a statement at 1:30 p.m. ET about what they described as military operations deep inside Saudi Arabia. The announcement itself offered no details about the operations or any impact on energy infrastructure.\n\nFor WTI and Brent, the next thing to watch is whether Wednesday’s larger flow through Hormuz can be sustained. Continued improvement would help ease some of the supply concerns. A renewed slowdown in traffic or confirmed damage to energy infrastructure could put the geopolitical risk premium back in focus.\n\n#### Kushner says Trump is open to Ukraine security guarantees\n\nOn Ukraine, US special envoy Jared Kushner said Trump came away from the Shenzhen meeting believing peace was achievable. Kushner said there had been progress on a postwar economic plan and that Russia had agreed to engage in a multilateral format with European countries. He added that Trump wants Europe alongside him in reaching a deal.\n\nKushner said Trump was open to an Article 5-style security guarantee for Ukraine, provided it served US interests. Any agreement would still have to spell out what the US and Europe would commit to if Ukraine came under attack again.\n\n#### Trump sets a Friday news conference\n\nTrump said he was heading back to Washington from China and would hold a White House news conference Friday at noon ET. He said he would also discuss trade deals with Thailand, the Philippines and other countries.\n\nYour market education doesn&#x27;t end here. Discover more insights and practical lessons in our investingLive video collection.\n\nADVERTISEMENT - CONTINUE READING BELOW\n\nAdvertisement\n\nAdvertisement\n\n## Must Read\n\n- [Nasdaq analysis after the much anticipated Nvidia earnings](https://investinglive.com/stocks/nasdaq-analysis-after-the-much-anticipated-nvidia-earnings/)\n\n- [Nvidia’s missing 10-Q: three reasons to be alert, not alarmed](https://investinglive.com/stocks/nvidia-s-missing-10-q-three-reasons-to-be-alert-not-alarmed/)\n\n- [Supplier, lender, shareholder: how Nvidia became the &quot;Bank of AI&quot;](https://investinglive.com/education/supplier-lender-shareholder-how-nvidia-became-the-bank-of-ai/)\n\n- [Recap: Japan exports hit record ¥11.8 trillion as AI chip demand extends run to 14 months](https://investinglive.com/news/recap-japan-exports-hit-record-11-8-trillion-as-ai-chip-demand-extends-run-to-14-months/)\n\n- [Zcash extends recovery but significant headwinds persist amid hawkish Fed and US-Iran tensions](http